  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The hydrocarbon of mass 72 is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub></math> . Since there is one monoclhoro derivative, the compound has twelve equivalent H's in four equivalent <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">′</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> . The compound is <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> (2,2-dimethylpropane) and the chloro derivative are as follows<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/16_soldad.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 53px;\" />",
